# ports.env - host port registry for the data-ops monorepo (committed, no secrets)
#
# The ONLY place a host (published) port is defined. Every compose file maps
#   "${<NAME>_HOST_PORT:?...}:<container port>"
# with no default, so a missing entry fails fast instead of silently guessing.
# The right-hand container port is set by the image and stays in the compose file.
#
# Loaded after .env by every Makefile (--env-file .env --env-file ports.env), so it
# always wins over stale values in .env. Plain `docker-compose` from the repo root
# needs: export COMPOSE_ENV_FILES=.env,ports.env  (the root Makefile does this).
#
# Rules: one line per published port, values unique across the repo.
# Check with: make ports   (lists ports, fails on duplicates / unused / undefined)

# --- databases (01-databases/) -----------------------------------------------
